location: HUMAN_RESOURCES_FEB_2026/project

Step 1. create environment in apps/backend (already in project)
Step 2: in project directory docker-compose up -d postgres backend
make sure that docker is installed
Step 3: activate env in apps/backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install asyncpg
Step 4: python init_db_fixed.py
Step 5: in project dir
docker-compose up -d orchestrator
Step 6: verify the containers
docker ps
Step 7: go to project/apps/web-employer
npm install
npm run dev


To run automatically:

Create a file named setup.sh in your root directory (/project/setup.sh) and paste this in(dont forget to chmod +x setup.sh):

#!/bin/bash

# 1. Setup Backend Environment
echo "🚀 Setting up Backend..."
cd apps/backend
if [ ! -f .env ]; then
    cp .env.example .env
    echo "⚠️ Created .env from example. PLEASE ADD YOUR OPENAI_API_KEY!"
fi

python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install asyncpg
cd ../..

# 2. Start Infrastructure
echo "🐳 Starting Docker (Postgres & Backend)..."
docker-compose up -d postgres backend

echo "⏳ Waiting 10s for Database to warm up..."
sleep 10

# 3. Initialize Database
echo "🏗️ Initializing Database Tables..."
cd apps/backend
source .venv/bin/activate
python init_db_fixed.py
cd ../..

# 4. Start AI Orchestrator
echo "🤖 Starting AI Orchestrator..."
docker-compose up -d orchestrator

# 5. Setup Frontend
echo "💻 Setting up Frontend..."
cd apps/web-employer
npm install

echo "✅ SETUP COMPLETE!"
echo "-------------------------------------------------------"
echo "Backend: http://localhost:8000/docs"
echo "Frontend: Run 'cd apps/web-employer && npm run dev'"
echo "-------------------------------------------------------"
docker ps
